# Day 40

## Experiment Title

Creating a Basic Workflow in GitHub Actions


## Objective

To create and execute a basic workflow using GitHub Actions.


## Theory

A workflow in GitHub Actions is a sequence of automated steps that run when specific events occur in a repository. Workflows are defined using YAML files stored inside the .github/workflows directory.

GitHub Actions workflows can automate tasks such as building applications, running tests, checking code quality, and deployment processes.


## Requirements

GitHub Account

GitHub Repository

GitHub Actions

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the GitHub repository.

Create a workflows directory inside the repository.

Create a YAML workflow configuration file.

Define workflow triggers and execution steps.

Commit and push the workflow file to the repository.

Observe workflow execution inside the GitHub Actions tab.


## Output

The GitHub Actions workflow was created successfully.

Workflow execution started automatically after pushing changes to the repository.

The workflow completed successfully without errors.


## Result

Successfully created and executed a basic workflow using GitHub Actions.
